Confirmed fixes:

Delete the nxpiw612-sdio line from the MACHINE_FEATURES:remove block in meta-karo-nxp/conf/layer.conf.
local.conf:
   MACHINE_FEATURES:append = " nxpiw612-sdio nxpwifi-all-sdio"
   DISTRO_FEATURES:append = " wifi"
   UBOOT_CONFIG = "default noenv mfg"
   IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " dropbear"
U-Boot: karo-minimal builds only noenv and mfg by default. The noenv variant ignores saveenv, which causes cold-boot failure. Flash u-boot-qsxp-ml81-default.bin to mmc0boot0.
Kernel config fragment: linux-karo uses kernel.bbclass and cml1.bbclass, not kernel-yocto. .cfg files in SRC_URI are not auto-merged, so cat them in do_configure:append(). CONFIG_CFG80211 is off by default. Without it you get “struct has no member ‘wdev’” errors.
NXP driver defaults: the nxp-wlan-sdk Makefile defaults to CONFIG_ANDROID_KERNEL=y, which disables cfg80211. Add this to both nxp-wlan-sdk_%.bbappend and kernel-module-nxp-wlan_%.bbappend:
   EXTRA_OEMAKE += "CONFIG_ANDROID_KERNEL=n CONFIG_STA_CFG80211=y CONFIG_UAP_CFG80211=y"
Devicetree: imx8mp-cmp9611-wifi.dtsi is #included from imx8mp-qsxp-ml81.dts. Ka-Ro’s overlay staging doesn’t copy unregistered files, so install the dtsi into ${S}/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/ via do_configure:append.
U-Boot env, once at first boot:
   setenv bootcmd_mmc run loadfdt loadkernel bootargs_mmc
   setenv append_bootargs root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 rw
   saveenv

Runtime:

Load with modprobe mlan, then modprobe moal fw_name=nxp/sd_w61x_v1.bin.se. The firmware family is w61x, not iw611. mlan0 appears afterwards.
Success looks like mmc1: new high speed SDIO card at address 0001 and driver string SDIW612---18.99.3.p21.10.
WiFi joined an AP with a DHCP lease, and dropbear works after modprobe.

UUU flash (uuu.auto):

MFG U-Boot u-boot-qsxp-ml81-mfg.bin (SDPS boot).
Production U-Boot u-boot-qsxp-ml81-default.bin goes to mmc0boot0.
Images: bootfs, rootfs and userfs .ext4 (karo-image-*-qsxp-ml81.ext4), with emmc_dev=0.
GPT layout: boot 64MB, rootfs 128MB, userfs MAX.

