Hardware

Board etched S001986C0, 1513.1 PHYTEC
Identified as a VM-117 phyCAM-M-mini module (ON Semi AR0521 sensor)
Cable marked AXON AWM 2896 80C VW-1
Target is 4-lane MIPI CSI-2

Pinout (from the phyCAM-M connector):

I2C on i2c2 (GPIO5_IO16-17). Default address 0x36, with GPIO1_IO29 as the address strap (low).
Reset on GPIO1_IO28.
CSI_*_A maps to &mipi_csi_0.
VCAM pin 5 is open (3.3V).
The module has its own 27MHz oscillator, so the SoC supplies no MCLK.

Decisions made

Use the mainline ar0521.c already in linux-karo 6.6.52 for the proof of concept, on the ISI raw Bayer path.
Defer PHYTEC’s vvcam/ISP-based phycam-ar0521.c port to a later goal.
The driver’s devm_clk_get(dev, "extclk") is mandatory and feeds its PLL math. Satisfy it with a fixed-clock node at the real oscillator frequency, even though the SoC doesn’t drive the pin.
Kconfig symbols (verified in source): CONFIG_VIDEO_AR0521, CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX8MQ_MIPI_CSI2, CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX8_ISI.
Still to tune: csis-hs-settle (placeholder 17). Adjust once frames appear, since garbage frames are the usual symptom of a wrong value.

