Lessons from the build failures

A bare labeled node like a fixed-clock is invalid at .dtsi top level. Wrap it in / { };.
The bbappend needs both FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend and SRC_URI +=. Confirm with bitbake -e linux-karo | grep ^SRC_URI=.
bitbake -c cleansstate linux-karo isn’t enough. Also rm -rf tmp/work-shared/qsxp-ml81/kernel-source/.
The dtsi had a missing < on the fsl,pins = < line in the pinctrl block. Find these with sed -n '60,70p' <file> | cat -A. Adding #include "imx8mp-pinfunc.h" was also done and is harmless.
Find the kernel source path with bitbake -e linux-karo | grep ^S=. It’s usually under tmp/work-shared/qsxp-ml81/kernel-source/, and edits there don’t persist across rebuilds.
