Diagnosing a firmware initialization failure on a module.

Firmware file is present and a reasonable size, so it’s not a missing-file problem — the driver got far enough to request and load it, then the module itself reported “Firmware Init Failed”. That’s the SDIW612/IW611 firmware failing to complete its own init handshake with the driver, not a driver-side error. This is a strong signal pointing at hardware sequencing rather than software — exactly the PDn#/reset ordering that was flagged as unverified against the datasheet, now potentially showing up as a real problem on a second board where timing might differ slightly.

Get the full surrounding context and check reset/PDn# state:

